{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794357169000-engineer-cc3-lowering-provenance.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\tCreated-GMT: 2026-11-11 06:40:00 GMT\n     2\tCreated-Local: 2026-11-11 13:40:00 +0700\n     3\tCoding-Agent: muse\n     4\tSession-ID: 32f932e8-e945-4e01-8a58-f044508a17e9\n     5\tModel: muse-wonder-1.0\n     6\tResumed-By: glm-5.3 (session e45fe836; muse died mid-round on two provider 429s - resume-by-state per 1794357400000-engineer-cc3-resume.prompt.md, 2026-11-11)\n     7\t\n     8\t# cc3 - lowering provenance & oracle C1 occurrence-key bridge: findings\n     9\t\n    10\tStatus: COMPLETE - all seven items landed and verified; the eight-file diff was audited\n    11\thunk-by-hunk, fixed where wrong (see the audit table below), and the full foreground\n    12\tbattery is green. Nothing committed.\n    13\t\n    14\t## PREFLIGHT BOUNDS (work item 7 - recorded BEFORE any tagged oracle run)\n    15\t\n    16\tMeasured 2026-11-11 by compiling the pinned binding fixture\n    17\t`{:call (latte-kernel.utils/vectorn? [1 2 3] 2)}` through `kernel-compile`\n    18\t(compile only; no C lane executed) and projecting its stamped tree through\n    19\tthe C1 encoder pipeline:\n    20\t\n    21\t| Bound | Value | Derivation |\n    22\t|---|---|---|\n    23\t| Canonical rows (stamped fixture tree) | 1,316 | `(:rows tree)` count |\n    24\t| Occurrences (all tree positions) | 3,669 | `vm/occurrences` |\n    25\t| Application occurrences A | 987 | `vm/application-occurrences` |\n    26\t| Oracle stamped guest sites (same tree) | 2 | `kernel-stamp-sites` rows - the coverage-separation gap in one line: the oracle set is 2 of 987 |\n    27\t| Max path depth (flattened steps) | 90 | max over application paths |\n    28\t| Total application path bytes | 103,650 | sum of `pr-str` lengths of application paths |\n    29\t| Guest instruction ceiling | 4,000,000 per C lane | RESTATED from `kernel-c` (`latte_oracle_test.clj:2484`, `run-guest-machine ... 4000000`); NOT raised |\n    30\t| Trace capacity | 1,000,000 records per C lane | RESTATED from the fixture program `(stream/make 1000000)`; NOT raised |\n    31\t| Worst trace record size | 29 bytes measured; 64 bytes declared ceiling | record `[fname arity caller-site]`: max guest fname 23 chars in the fixture forms, arity and site id are small integers; declared ceiling allows fname <= 40 chars, arity <= 999, site < 10^6 |\n    32\t| Trace byte bound | 64,000,000 bytes per lane | 1,000,000 records x 64-byte declared ceiling; drain is after halt (`tu/drain`), so peak retained = capacity |\n    33\t| Binding added guest work | 0 instructions, 0 trace records | the cc3 binding is static/test-side: it reads the already-compiled tree and the already-derived site table; it neither re-stamps nor re-instruments, so the 4,000,000 / 1,000,000 ceilings are occupied exactly as before (the older binding fixture measured 2,024,912 walker / 1,105,792 semantic steps, recorded at `latte_oracle_test.clj:3216`; under both ceilings) |\n    34\t\n    35\tFailure rule: a tagged run that exceeds any ceiling above is a failed\n    36\tbounded run; bounds are never silently raised (design 6.3).\n    37\t\n    38\tBounds verification (resume session, 2026-11-11): every number above was\n    39\tre-measured compile-only and matches EXACTLY - 1,316 / 3,669 / 987 stamped-tree\n    40\tcounts, 80 raw path steps / 90 flattened, 103,650 path bytes, 2 oracle sites.\n    41\tDerivation-basis note: the table rows/occurrences/applications are the\n    42\tSTAMPED-tree counts (the larger tree the C lanes execute); the C1 coverage\n    43\tequality of item 6 holds over the pre-stamp COMPILED tree (measured 1,309 rows /\n    44\t3,649 occurrences / 981 applications). One citation corrected from the stub:\n    45\tthe occupancy reference note lives at `latte_oracle_test.clj:3216`, not :2454.\n    46\t\n    47\t## Per-item disposition\n    48\t\n    49\t### 1. Semantic row provenance - LANDED (one audit fix)\n    50\t\n    51\t- `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc:188` `validated-call-origins`: the\n    52\t  `{[root path] origin}` map a C1 side table claims over the canonical tree.\n    53\t  Per-occurrence resolution: each row's origin is THAT occurrence's own - a\n    54\t  tree mixing `[:source ...]` and `[:expansion ...]` applications is never\n    55\t  stamped with one blanket origin. Every row is held to the contract before\n    56\t  it is believed: malformed row / unsupported marker version /\n    57\t  non-occurrence origin (`[:oracle/fixture <id>]` included) / foreign\n    58\t  root / path naming no `:application` occurrence of this tree refuses with\n    59\t  `:rule :call-site-row`; two rows for one occurrence refuse with\n    60\t  `:rule :call-site-conflict`. Non-`:yang/call-site` frontend metadata in\n    61\t  the same relation is neither believed nor refused. An occurrence with no\n    62\t  row is simply absent (absence, never invention).\n    63\t- `linearize.cljc:230` `project-rows` (3-arity; `:273` `:call-provenance`):\n    64\t  `[[pc origin root path] ...]`, one row per `:call` instruction, joined\n    65\t  through `flatten-tree`'s own `sources` paths (the same 2.5-path grammar as\n    66\t  `vm/occurrences` and `vm/application-occurrences` - the green join\n    67\t  verifies the conventions agree). Rule R applications lower to `:define`\n    68\t  and yield no call row. The caller still supplies the segment coordinate\n    69\t  (unchanged contract); the vector and its address are identical with or\n    70\t  without the side table (asserted).\n    71\t- AUDIT FIX (mine): the interrupted code stamped `:call-provenance` with the\n    72\t  caller-supplied single `origin` when no side table was given - exactly the\n    73\t  one-origin-across-the-set stamping the mob condition forbids. Removed:\n    74\t  `:call-provenance` is non-empty ONLY from validated C1 rows; the full\n    75\t  `:provenance` table keeps carrying the caller's origin as before.\n    76\t  Red-first: new assertions failed against the fallback (evidence below).\n    77\t- Test: `test/yin/vm/semantic/linearize_test.cljc:398`\n    78\t  `call-provenance-resolves-per-occurrence-origins` - mixed origins resolved\n    79\t  per occurrence, Rule R absence, partial-table absence, canonical\n    80\t  invariance, four refusal arms. AUDIT FIX (mine): the `[:oracle/fixture 1]`\n    81\t  refusal arm had a bracket typo (the row was unwrapped - its ELEMENTS were\n    82\t  passed as five separate rows, all filtered, so the refusal never fired and\n    83\t  the interrupted session's own test was red against its own code); wrapped.\n    84\t\n    85\t### 2. Native image provenance - LANDED\n    86\t\n    87\t- `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc:60` `call-key-map`: validates a\n    88\t  `:call-provenance` relation against the vector it claims - a row naming a\n    89\t  pc that holds no `:call` in THAT vector refuses `:rule :call-provenance`.\n    90\t  PC equality across formats is never assumed.\n    91\t- `derive.cljc:79` `stack-image` (2-arity): reconstructs call provenance\n    92\t  through the stack derivation's OWN pc mapping (the recorded pc is the\n    93\t  stack pc where the `:call` lands, after operand pushes). Adds a\n    94\t  `{:kind :call :source pc :origin o :root r :path p}` side-table diagnostic\n    95\t  at each call pc - the existing `:closure`/`:var` diagnostic shapes are\n    96\t  undisturbed (asserted).\n    97\t- `derive.cljc:193` `register-image` (2-arity): layout preserved, so a\n    98\t  semantic `:call` pc IS the register pc; rows\n    99\t  `[segment-address pc origin root path]`.\n   100\t- Both images are byte-identical with or without provenance (asserted\n   101\t  against the 1-arity derivations).\n   102\t- Test: `test/yin/vm/semantic/derive_test.cljc:832`\n   103\t  `native-images-reconstruct-call-provenance`. AUDIT FIX (mine): its refusal\n   104\t  arm used a bare `(catch Exception ...)` in a `.cljc` - clj-kondo's cljs\n   105\t  analysis errors on it (recorded red); replaced with the file's portable\n   106\t  conditional.\n   107\t\n   108\t### 3. Durable persistence - LANDED (one audit fix)\n   109\t\n   110\t- `src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:325-345`: a C1-claiming publication\n   111\t  projects WITH its validated rows (`project-rows tree nil (:rows claim)`)\n   112\t  so every image's call provenance is resolved per-occurrence at lowering\n   113\t  time; an unclaimed publication projects exactly as before. The stack image\n   114\t  hashed into the manifest is the same derivation (`:image` selected; the\n   115\t  register image with `:call-provenance` dissoc'd) - manifest, hashes and\n   116\t  addresses unchanged.\n   117\t- `publish.cljc:386-420`: the instruction-provenance relation\n   118\t  `{:yin.vm.provenance/schema 1 :root ... :semantic [[seg pc origin root path] ...] :stack [...] :register [...]}`\n   119\t  is materialized as a SIDE ARTIFACT outside the schema-1 manifest hash (the\n   120\t  cc1 precedent: the `:yang.call-site` record names manifest, table, and now\n   121\t  `:yang.call-site/provenance`; the manifest never names the record -\n   122\t  asserted in the test).\n   123\t- `publish.cljc:536` `published-instruction-provenance`: retrieval held to\n   124\t  the same manifest/root linkage as `published-call-site-table`; nil when no\n   125\t  record verifies or the publication claimed no C1 - legacy unannotated\n   126\t  publications persist none and remain fully loadable (tested).\n   127\t- `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:158` `packet->projection`: the choke point that\n   128\t  used to select `(:vector ...)` and discard the rest now keeps the full\n   129\t  projection (`packet->vector` delegates; behavior unchanged).\n   130\t- `repl.cljc:171` `packet-call-provenance`: resolves an expanded packet's\n   131\t  three images' call provenance from the expander's RETAINED tables\n   132\t  (`call-site-tables`, keyed `[admission-origin final-root]`); a root claimed\n   133\t  by two retained admissions refuses `:rule :ambiguous-call-site-table` (a\n   134\t  table is never borrowed across admissions); a root with no retained table\n   135\t  answers nil (absence, never invention). Segment coordinates are the\n   136\t  images' own content identities as the loaders compute them\n   137\t  (`ucf/code-address`, `dcode/image-hash`, `rcode/register-hash`).\n   138\t- AUDIT FIX (mine): the function derived each image twice (once to hash,\n   139\t  once with provenance). Now each image is derived once with provenance\n   140\t  attached; its own (unchanged) hash is patched into the rows afterward -\n   141\t  same values, half the derivations, the publish-side pattern.\n   142\t- Tests: `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:1968`\n   143\t  `published-instruction-provenance-test` (persistence outside the manifest,\n   144\t  every persisted row a claimed occurrence key, all three lanes non-empty\n   145\t  where calls exist, the manifest's closed schema-1 key set, legacy\n   146\t  loadability) and `:2012` `repl-packet-call-provenance-test`\n   147\t  (retained-table resolution, absence, ambiguity refusal). AUDIT FIX (mine):\n   148\t  the ambiguity arm's inline catch spelled the reader conditional so that\n   149\t  on the cljd platform the `:default` branch matched BEFORE `:cljd`,\n   150\t  yielding the keyword `:default` as the catch type; replaced with the\n   151\t  file's own `failure-rule` helper.\n   152\t\n   153\t### 4. Datom lane decision - RESTRICTION (D1's stated dependency)\n   154\t\n   155\t`project-datoms` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc:349`) keeps its\n   156\t`[pc entity]` provenance and carries NO occurrence key K. The\n   157\tentity-to-occurrence bridge (design 2.4: explicit entity-to-occurrence\n   158\tmapping with owning batch/root/path, refusing ambiguity;\n   159\t`encoder/datom-entity-occurrences` is the starting machinery) is DEFERRED TO\n   160\tD1 AS ITS STATED DEPENDENCY; until it lands, cc3's provenance claims cover\n   161\tthe ROW LANE ONLY, and the datom lane's `[pc entity]` shape must not be\n   162\tread as a K bridge. Recorded in the `project-datoms` docstring and pinned by\n   163\t`test/yin/vm/semantic/linearize_test.cljc:463`\n   164\t`datom-lane-provenance-names-entities-only`. A restriction, not a silent\n   165\tgap.\n   166\t\n   167\t### 5. Oracle binding - LANDED (two audit fixes)\n   168\t\n   169\t- `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2472`: `kernel-compile` now retains\n   170\t  `:compiled-ast` - the CHRONOLOGY condition (mob condition 2): compilation\n   171\t  happens FIRST, stamping by insertion AFTERWARD, so the binding is derived\n   172\t  from the pre-stamp compiled tree's validated C1 rows while the site ids\n   173\t  are read off the stamped tree (stamping wraps argument nodes in place;\n   174\t  every other node keeps its path - the bijection's\n   175\t  `(every? marked (vals binding))` assertion verifies that path alignment at\n   176\t  runtime, every run).\n   177\t- `:3427` `cc3-walk` (row-grammar paths over a map AST - the same positions\n   178\t  as `vm/occurrences`), `:3450` `cc3-stamp-site-id`, `:3458`\n   179\t  `cc3-oracle-binding`: each stamped oracle integer site maps to its\n   180\t  post-expansion C1 key K = [origin root path] with origin\n   181\t  `[:source :program <canonical-source-hash> 0]` - a RECORDED admission\n   182\t  coordinate in `vm.cljc:938-958`'s validator shape (asserted\n   183\t  `vm/occurrence-origin?`); `[:oracle/fixture <id>]` alone is never\n   184\t  minted (asserted false).\n   185\t- `:3502` `test-cc3-oracle-site-c1-binding`: the tagged deftest. Verified:\n   186\t  (a) bijection - the stamped sites equal the binding's keys, no two sites\n   187\t  share one occurrence (distinct-vals), every bound key is a validated C1\n   188\t  occurrence; (b) BOTH C LANES (walker, semantic) run the SAME stamped\n   189\t  artifact under the recorded ceilings and every EXECUTED site id resolves\n   190\t  through the binding to the IDENTICAL K set in both lanes (2 sites each);\n   191\t  (c) Rule R - `:define` paths never appear as call-provenance keys.\n   192\t- AUDIT FIXES (mine): (1) the lowering block's `keys-of` destructured the\n   193\t  4-element semantic rows `[pc origin root path]` with the 5-element native\n   194\t  shape, comparing `[root path nil]` garbage against `[origin root path]` -\n   195\t  a permanent self-inequality (recorded red: 2 failures at :3552/:3553);\n   196\t  fixed with `sem-keys` for the 4-element rows. (2) the no-two-sites check\n   197\t  was `(= (count binding) (count (vals binding)))` - vacuously true for ANY\n   198\t  map; fixed to `(= (count binding) (count (into #{} (vals binding))))`.\n   199\t\n   200\t### 6. Coverage separation - LANDED\n   201\t\n   202\tThe same deftest verifies the two relations SEPARATELY:\n   203\t- The complete C1 set: `(= eligible marked)` - every final application\n   204\t  occurrence of the compiled tree carries exactly its marker (981\n   205\t  applications over the compiled tree; the fixture's library wrapping and\n   206\t  generated calls included; 987 counted on the stamped tree).\n   207\t- The oracle set: 2 sites of 981 - the strict-inequality assertion pins\n   208\t  that uncredited helpers, duplicate-content occurrences and\n   209\t  transformation-generated applications are C1 occurrences but NOT oracle\n   210\t  sites (the bijection is oracle-site to its selected compiled occurrence,\n   211\t  never the full set).\n   212\t\n   213\t### 7. Preflight bounds - recorded, then verified\n   214\t\n   215\tThe bounds table above was recorded by the interrupted session BEFORE any\n   216\ttagged run (compile-only measurement). The resume session re-measured every\n   217\tnumber compile-only - all match exactly - and the tagged run then executed\n   218\tunder the restated 4,000,000 / 1,000,000 ceilings (neither raised; the\n   219\tbinding adds 0 guest instructions and 0 trace records; both lanes\n   220\t`:completed`).\n   221\t\n   222\t## Audit of the interrupted session's diff (resume-by-state, hunk-by-hunk)\n   223\t\n   224\tThe eight-file diff was structurally sound but had NEVER BEEN RUN. Eight\n   225\tdefects found and fixed (details at the items above):\n   226\t\n   227\t| # | Where | Defect | Disposition |\n   228\t|---|---|---|---|\n   229\t| 1 | linearize.cljc `project-rows` | blanket-origin fallback stamped `:call-provenance` across all calls when no side table given - the exact forbidden one-origin-across-the-set | removed, red-first (assertions added, red recorded, fix, green) |\n   230\t| 2 | linearize_test.clj oracle-fixture refusal arm | bracket typo splatted the row into five non-rows - the arm never fired; the session's own test was red against its own code | row wrapped; green |\n   231\t| 3 | latte_oracle_test.clj lowering block | `keys-of` shape mismatch - permanent self-inequality | `sem-keys` destructure for 4-element rows; green |\n   232\t| 4 | latte_oracle_test.clj bijection | vacuous count-vs-vals check (always true for any map) | distinct-vals set count |\n   233\t| 5 | derive_test.clj:878 | bare `(catch Exception ...)` in `.cljc` - kondo cljs error | file's portable conditional; kondo red recorded |\n   234\t| 6 | clojure_callsite_test.cljc ambiguity arm | inline reader conditional where `:default` shadows `:cljd` (keyword `:default` as catch type on cljd) | the file's `failure-rule` helper |\n   235\t| 7 | repl.cljc `packet-call-provenance` | each image derived twice (hash pass + provenance pass) | single derivation, coordinate patched after |\n   236\t| 8 | linearize_test.cljc:410 | unused binding `by-path` (kondo warning) | removed |\n   237\t\n   238\tEverything else in the diff audited correct as written: the path-grammar\n   239\tjoin (linearize flatten-tree, vm/occurrences, encoder side tables), the\n   240\tstamping chronology handling, the publish-side out-of-hash placement, the\n   241\trefusal rules, the legacy-loadability paths, and the walker/semantic lane\n   242\tassertions.\n   243\t\n   244\t## Red-first evidence\n   245\t\n   246\t1. Fallback removal (audit #1): new assertions that a bare caller origin\n   247\t   yields EMPTY `:call-provenance` were RED against the interrupted code\n   248\t   (recorded: FAIL at linearize_test.cljc:443, actual showed both call pcs\n   249\t   blanket-stamped `[[3 [:source :medium :batch 0] ... [[3 0]]] [6 ... []]]`),\n   250\t   GREEN after the fix.\n   251\t2. Items 1-3 src surfaces: the four new deftests RED with the four src\n   252\t   files reverted to HEAD - linearize/derive:\n   253\t   `ArityException: Wrong number of args (3) passed to: project-rows`;\n   254\t   callsite namespace: compile failure\n   255\t   `No such var: publish/published-instruction-provenance` (covers both the\n   256\t   publish and repl tests). Restored, all green.\n   257\t3. Portability fix (audit #5): clj-kondo reported\n   258\t   `derive_test.cljc:878:28: error: Unresolved symbol: Exception` with the\n   259\t   bare catch (recorded), 0 errors after.\n   260\t4. Oracle test fixes (audits #2/#3): the pre-fix tagged run's two\n   261\t   recorded failures at :3552/:3553 (keys-of self-inequality) and the\n   262\t   pre-fix linearize-test failure at the oracle-fixture arm are the red;\n   263\t   the re-runs are green.\n   264\t\n   265\t## Verification (foreground, explicit timeouts, nothing backgrounded at landing)\n   266\t\n   267\t| Lane | Command | Outcome |\n   268\t|---|---|---|\n   269\t| The battery | `clojure -M:test -n yang.clojure-callsite-test` | 33 tests, 379 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n   270\t| Touched semantic namespace | `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.semantic.linearize-test` | 24 tests, 1,121 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n   271\t| Touched derive namespace | `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.semantic.derive-test` | 27 tests, 6,212 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n   272\t| Oracle (narrow selection: binding + bijection + refusals) | `clojure -M:test -n yang.latte-oracle-test -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-cc3-oracle-site-c1-binding` | 1 test, 20 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors - both C lanes `:completed`, every executed site bound, identical K sets |\n   273\t| repl safety (packet-to-vector refactor) | `clojure -M:test -n yin.repl-test` | 52 tests, 268 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors |\n   274\t| kondo (all 8 changed files) | `clj-kondo --lint` over the 8 files (via the ProcessBuilder lane; `clojure -M:kondo` is approval-gated in this worktree) | errors: 0, warnings: 0 |\n   275\t\n   276\tPublish's touched tests live in the callsite battery (the cc2 pattern:\n   277\t`publish-module!` / `published-call-site-table` coverage is there). The kit\n   278\tcontract test is N/A on this laptop (three measured non-completions, logged)\n   279\tand is covered by shiva at landing, per the brief.\n   280\t\n   281\t## Invariants\n   282\t\n   283\t- Zero canonical change: vector + address identical with/without the side\n   284\t  table (linearize test); stack/register images byte-identical with/without\n   285\t  provenance (derive test); manifest stays the closed schema-1 key set with\n   286\t  unchanged hashes and addresses (callsite test).\n   287\t- Legacy unannotated packets remain fully loadable (callsite test; the\n   288\t  retrieval answers nil; code paths untouched).\n   289\t- Origins never minted: `validated-call-origins` refuses every non-origin\n   290\t  shape; the oracle binding uses only a validator-shaped RECORDED admission\n   291\t  coordinate; metadata never enters rows, CBOR, or hashing (side artifacts\n   292\t  only, outside the manifest hash).\n   293\t\n   294\t## Owner-visible items\n   295\t\n   296\t1. dht forwarding need (the cc2 custody item, closed on the publish side):\n   297\t   `dht/publish-name!` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/dht.cljc:70`) still\n   298\t   select-keyses `[:address :links]` and discards the publication result's\n   299\t   `:call-sites` handle - which now carries `:provenance` beside `:record`\n   300\t   and `:table`. dht.cljc is forbidden to this round, and the fix does NOT\n   301\t   require editing it: the publish side exposes the full retained handle\n   302\t   (`publish-closure!`'s result `:call-sites {:record ... :table ...\n   303\t   :provenance ...}`). The one-line forwarding need for the dht owner: add\n   304\t   `:call-sites` to dht.cljc:70's select-keys (or forward the record\n   305\t   address) so DHT publications retain their provenance handle.\n   306\t2. D1 dependency (the datom-lane restriction, item 4) - restated: the\n   307\t   entity-to-occurrence bridge is D1's to land; cc3's claims are row-lane\n   308\t   only.\n   309\t\n   310\t## Unverified items\n   311\t\n   312\t- The suite-scale battery and the kit contract test: shiva at landing (per\n   313\t  the brief; not run here).\n   314\t- The full oracle suite: shiva-scale; only the cc3 deftest ran (per the\n   315\t  brief).\n   316\t- cljs/cljd lanes: not run on this laptop (JVM-only verification per the\n   317\t  brief). The portable-catch fixes exist to keep those lanes compilable;\n   318\t  verified by kondo's dual clj/cljs analysis (0 errors), not by a lane run.\n   319\t- `src/dev/latte_oracle_tables.clj` regeneration: untouched by cc3 (evidence\n   320\t  regeneration is D1's round, R7) - the binding reads compiled fixtures\n   321\t  directly and writes no evidence files.\n   322\t- Four-host publication blast radius (design 3.3): prelude republication on\n   323\t  Node/Dart/Jolt is a D1/cc4 concern; this round's publication changes are\n   324\t  additive side artifacts only.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc | sed -n '1,310p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.semantic.derive\n     2\t  \"Pure native derivations from the admitted semantic register vector A.\"\n     3\t  (:refer-clojure :exclude [resolve])\n     4\t  (:require [yin.vm.semantic.code :as code]\n     5\t            [yin.vm.debruijn :as db]\n     6\t            [yin.vm.semantic.analysis :as analysis]\n     7\t            [yin.vm.debruijn-register-code :as rcode]))\n     8\t\n     9\t\n    10\t(defn- chains\n    11\t  [v bodies]\n    12\t  (letfn [(chain\n    13\t            [i]\n    14\t            (if-let [owner (:owner (nth bodies i))]\n    15\t              (into [(nth (nth v owner) 2)]\n    16\t                    (chain (code/body-index bodies owner)))\n    17\t              []))]\n    18\t    (mapv chain (range (count bodies)))))\n    19\t\n    20\t\n    21\t(defn resolve\n    22\t  \"Rewrite only variables and closure binders. The result is an unhashed\n    23\t   stage value; pcs and virtual registers are preserved.\"\n    24\t  [v]\n    25\t  (let [bodies (code/parse v)\n    26\t        frames (chains v bodies)\n    27\t        names (volatile! {})]\n    28\t    {:vector\n    29\t     (mapv (fn [pc]\n    30\t             (let [[op rd x y :as t] (nth v pc)]\n    31\t               (case op\n    32\t                 :var (let [{:keys [bound free]}\n    33\t                            (db/resolve-name (nth frames (code/body-index bodies pc)) x)]\n    34\t                        (if bound\n    35\t                          (do (vswap! names assoc pc x)\n    36\t                              (into [:load-bound rd] bound))\n    37\t                          [:load-free rd free]))\n    38\t                 :closure [:closure rd (count x) y]\n    39\t                 t)))\n    40\t           (range (count v)))\n    41\t     :bodies bodies\n    42\t     :name