{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'call-site-tables|call-site-admissions|materialize\"'!|durable|program-out'\"' src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc | head -75; nl -ba /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794357169000-engineer-cc3-lowering-provenance.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md | sed -n '10,47p'; cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794357400000-engineer-cc3-resume.glm-5.3.stdout.log; rg -n '\"'^diff|''^@@'\"' /tmp/cc3-review-diff.txt\"","aggregated_output":"7:   expander observes, and `program-out`, which the evaluator's own observer\n174:   (`call-site-tables`, keyed `[admission-origin final-root]`):\n184:        tables (:call-site-tables (:expander state))\n263:  \"The loader the evaluator observer hands each `program-out` value, per\n275:   ;; producer of `program-out` is the expander, so each supplies the\n791:   `program-out` writer.  No log writer: `(compile ...)` renders events.\"\n792:  [program-identity program-out]\n797:    program-out))\n809:   `:observer` — and appends each expanded tree packet to `program-out` —\n812:   (`yin.repl.index`) is a peer attached to `program-out` beside it; the\n827:   A durable store's HEAD write travels with the store handle\n836:        program-out (make-attachment ingress-capacity)]\n842:     :expander (make-expander (:identity program-in) (:stream program-out))\n843:     :call-site-admissions {}\n844:     :row-stream (:stream program-out)\n845:     :row-observer (:observer program-out)\n846:     :indexer (index/make-indexer {:observer ((:attach program-out))\n851:     :ast-indexer (ast-index/make-indexer {:observer ((:attach program-out))})\n916:   `{:type :file :dir dir}`, the durable content log at\n924:   `:index-recovery` carries what the durable open recovered —\n929:   mints a new token for its own.  In durable mode `(reset)` and `(vm …)`\n934:   durable directory store with a `dao.jing.dht` node composed over it.\n1235:  \"Drive the code indexer's observer over `program-out`: it commits each\n1244:  \"Drive the AST indexer's observer over `program-out`: it adds each\n1262:(defn call-site-tables\n1267:   `:call-site-tables` option). Nil before any claimed expansion.\"\n1269:  (:call-site-tables (:expander state)))\n1272:(defn call-site-admissions\n1280:   `:call-site-admissions` option). No counter is compared: a program\n1290:  (:call-site-admissions state))\n1325:(defn- record-call-site-admissions\n1350:                          (or (call-site-tables state) {}))\n1371:                             (not (contains? (:call-site-admissions st)\n1373:                      (assoc-in st [:call-site-admissions\n1377:                (update state :call-site-admissions #(or % {}))\n1383:   each observed batch and appends the tree packet to `program-out`; a\n1395:  \"Drive the evaluator's observer over `program-out`: it loads each\n1397:   output medium.  The two stages meet only at `program-out`; neither calls\n1483:   :call-site-tables (call-site-tables state)\n1484:   :call-site-admissions (call-site-admissions state)\n1831:          tables-before (call-site-tables state')\n1860:                                     (record-call-site-admissions\n2028:   Over a durable store the code index is not the session's to drop: the\n2041:           (store/durable? (:index-store state))\n2099:                   (if (store/durable? (:index-store state))\n2100:                     \" (VM store cleared; durable code index kept)\"\n    10\tStatus: COMPLETE - all seven items landed and verified; the eight-file diff was audited\n    11\thunk-by-hunk, fixed where wrong (see the audit table below), and the full foreground\n    12\tbattery is green. Nothing committed.\n    13\t\n    14\t## PREFLIGHT BOUNDS (work item 7 - recorded BEFORE any tagged oracle run)\n    15\t\n    16\tMeasured 2026-11-11 by compiling the pinned binding fixture\n    17\t`{:call (latte-kernel.utils/vectorn? [1 2 3] 2)}` through `kernel-compile`\n    18\t(compile only; no C lane executed) and projecting its stamped tree through\n    19\tthe C1 encoder pipeline:\n    20\t\n    21\t| Bound | Value | Derivation |\n    22\t|---|---|---|\n    23\t| Canonical rows (stamped fixture tree) | 1,316 | `(:rows tree)` count |\n    24\t| Occurrences (all tree positions) | 3,669 | `vm/occurrences` |\n    25\t| Application occurrences A | 987 | `vm/application-occurrences` |\n    26\t| Oracle stamped guest sites (same tree) | 2 | `kernel-stamp-sites` rows - the coverage-separation gap in one line: the oracle set is 2 of 987 |\n    27\t| Max path depth (flattened steps) | 90 | max over application paths |\n    28\t| Total application path bytes | 103,650 | sum of `pr-str` lengths of application paths |\n    29\t| Guest instruction ceiling | 4,000,000 per C lane | RESTATED from `kernel-c` (`latte_oracle_test.clj:2484`, `run-guest-machine ... 4000000`); NOT raised |\n    30\t| Trace capacity | 1,000,000 records per C lane | RESTATED from the fixture program `(stream/make 1000000)`; NOT raised |\n    31\t| Worst trace record size | 29 bytes measured; 64 bytes declared ceiling | record `[fname arity caller-site]`: max guest fname 23 chars in the fixture forms, arity and site id are small integers; declared ceiling allows fname <= 40 chars, arity <= 999, site < 10^6 |\n    32\t| Trace byte bound | 64,000,000 bytes per lane | 1,000,000 records x 64-byte declared ceiling; drain is after halt (`tu/drain`), so peak retained = capacity |\n    33\t| Binding added guest work | 0 instructions, 0 trace records | the cc3 binding is static/test-side: it reads the already-compiled tree and the already-derived site table; it neither re-stamps nor re-instruments, so the 4,000,000 / 1,000,000 ceilings are occupied exactly as before (the older binding fixture measured 2,024,912 walker / 1,105,792 semantic steps, recorded at `latte_oracle_test.clj:3216`; under both ceilings) |\n    34\t\n    35\tFailure rule: a tagged run that exceeds any ceiling above is a failed\n    36\tbounded run; bounds are never silently raised (design 6.3).\n    37\t\n    38\tBounds verification (resume session, 2026-11-11): every number above was\n    39\tre-measured compile-only and matches EXACTLY - 1,316 / 3,669 / 987 stamped-tree\n    40\tcounts, 80 raw path steps / 90 flattened, 103,650 path bytes, 2 oracle sites.\n    41\tDerivation-basis note: the table rows/occurrences/applications are the\n    42\tSTAMPED-tree counts (the larger tree the C lanes execute); the C1 coverage\n    43\tequality of item 6 holds over the pre-stamp COMPILED tree (measured 1,309 rows /\n    44\t3,649 occurrences / 981 applications). One citation corrected from the stub:\n    45\tthe occupancy reference note lives at `latte_oracle_test.clj:3216`, not :2454.\n    46\t\n    47\t## Per-item disposition\n[claude-code:unrecognized_model] {\"model\":\"glm-5.3\",\"query_source\":\"sdk\"}\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-11-11 05:07:09 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-11 12:07:09 +07\n\n# cc3 resume-by-state — round complete\n\nThe interrupted muse session's eight-file diff was audited hunk-by-hunk, fixed, and verified; all seven items are landed. Nothing committed.\n\n## What the audit found\n\nThe diff was structurally sound but **had never been run**. Eight defects, all fixed:\n\n| # | Where | Defect |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `linearize.cljc` `project-rows` | blanket-origin fallback stamped `:call-provenance` across all calls when no C1 side table given — the exact \"one origin across the set\" the mob forbids. Removed, red-first (assertions red against the fallback, recorded, then green). |\n| 2 | `linearize_test.cljc` oracle-fixture arm | bracket typo splatted the row into five non-rows — the refusal never fired; the session's **own test was red against its own code** (this is what first exposed the never-run state). |\n| 3 | `latte_oracle_test.clj` lowering block | `keys-of` destructured 4-element semantic rows with the 5-element native shape — permanent self-inequality (2 recorded failures). |\n| 4 | `latte_oracle_test.clj` bijection | vacuous `(= (count binding) (count (vals binding)))` — always true; now a distinct-vals check. |\n| 5 | `derive_test.cljc:878` | bare `(catch Exception …)` in `.cljc` — kondo cljs error (red recorded); now the file's portable conditional. |\n| 6 | `clojure_callsite_test.cljc` | reader conditional where `:default` shadows `:cljd`; now the file's `failure-rule`. |\n| 7 | `repl.cljc` | each image derived twice; now once, coordinate patched after. |\n| 8 | `linearize_test.cljc:410` | unused binding (kondo warning); removed. |\n\n## Verification (all green)\n\n- **Battery** `yang.clojure-callsite-test` — 33 tests / 379 assertions\n- **Touched namespaces** — linearize 24/1,121 · derive 27/6,212 · repl safety 52/268\n- **Oracle (narrow, tagged run)** `test-cc3-oracle-site-c1-binding` — 1 test / 20 assertions, both C lanes `:completed`, every executed site bound, identical K sets across lanes\n- **kondo** all 8 changed files — 0 errors, 0 warnings\n- **Preflight bounds** re-measured compile-only: every recorded number exact (1,316/3,669/987/2/90/103,650); ceilings 4M/1M restated, not raised; one citation corrected (`:3216`, not `:2454`)\n\n## Decisions recorded\n\n- **Datom lane: RESTRICTION** — `[pc entity]` carries no K; the entity→occurrence bridge is D1's stated dependency (docstring + pinning test + findings).\n- **dht custody item** closed on the publish side (the result now exposes `:call-sites {:record :table :provenance}`); the one-line forwarding need at `dht.cljc:70` is recorded as owner-visible.\n\n## Deliverable\n\nThe findings are complete at the **worktree mirror** `collab/yang-clojure/1794357169000-engineer-cc3-lowering-provenance.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md` (the main-checkout path was off-limits per this round's instructions, sandbox-denied verbatim as the brief anticipates). Unverified items (shiva-scale suite, kit contract test, cljs/cljd lanes, four-host blast radius) are