{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'packet-call-provenance' src test; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/dht.cljc | sed -n '54,78p'; nl -ba collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md | sed -n '310,340p'; rg -n '\"'^(diff --git|'\"\\\\+[\"'^+])'\"' /tmp/cc3-review-diff.txt | tail -12; nl -ba test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj | sed -n '3205,3223p'\"","aggregated_output":"test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:2012:(deftest repl-packet-call-provenance-test\ntest/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:2027:    (let [prov (repl/packet-call-provenance state packet)]\ntest/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:2033:    (is (nil? (repl/packet-call-provenance {:expander {}} packet))\ntest/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc:2038:               (repl/packet-call-provenance\nsrc/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:171:(defn packet-call-provenance\n    54\t  \"Publish the module `name` exporting `exports`, derived from the\n    55\t   publisher's own index `db` (`module-from-index`, section 5.3), through\n    56\t   the node's store, and sign what binds the name to it (6.6): answers\n    57\t   `{:status :ok :address a :links {...} :envelopes [...]}`, each envelope\n    58\t   `publish/assertion`'s answer, for the caller to enter into its index\n    59\t   as one transaction (6.1) before it announces.  Without `key` it is\n    60\t   refused `:yin.link.publish/no-key`; any refusal writes nothing.\n    61\t   `opts` also carries `module-from-index`'s `:primitives`, `:modules`\n    62\t   and `:host-modules`.\"\n    63\t  [node db {:keys [key name] :as opts}]\n    64\t  (if-not key\n    65\t    (refused :yin.link.publish/no-key {:name name})\n    66\t    (let [spec (publish/module-from-index db opts)\n    67\t          res (if (= :refused (:status spec)) spec (publish! node spec))]\n    68\t      (if (= :refused (:status res))\n    69\t        res\n    70\t        (assoc (select-keys res [:address :links])\n    71\t               :status :ok\n    72\t               :envelopes (publish/name-envelopes db key name (:address res)))))))\n    73\t\n    74\t\n    75\t;; =============================================================================\n    76\t;; The module load (4.3)\n    77\t;; =============================================================================\n    78\t\n   310\tAlso compare the oracle's existing two-field tracing with T to isolate the extra caller-site field from the original body-entry instrumentation. Report S−B and T−S separately, and the old-trace→tagged-trace delta. If instrumentation itself changes code, keep its canonical image and compile cost separate from side-only annotation. Static C1 must change **zero canonical code bytes/addresses and zero guest instructions** for otherwise identical input; runtime tracing has no such zero-cost claim.\n   311\t\n   312\tMeasure cold and warm compile/load/query separately; use fresh publication caches for cold tests, fixed workload/repetition count and host/version, and publish distribution plus raw samples rather than an unqualified single timing. Report query indexes/build time separately from query execution. Do not call a host trace hook “zero overhead” because guest instruction count did not increase.\n   313\t\n   314\t### 6.3 Bounds published before any tagged run\n   315\t\n   316\tThe implementation preflight record must contain actual finite numbers (no “TBD”, unlimited trace, or post-run adjustment) for:\n   317\t\n   318\t| Bound | Required derivation / failure |\n   319\t|---|---|\n   320\t| Maximum input rows, occurrences, A, D and total path bytes | Derive from the pinned static corpus; reject over-bound traversal before instrumentation. Include generated/bundled prelude expansion, not only source calls. |\n   321\t| Static side bytes and retained memory | Measure S without tracing; declare maximum per artifact/module and aggregate closure. Serialization size may be computed exactly before execution. Stop/revise on exceeding the declared storage/memory bound. |\n   322\t| Maximum records E and trace capacity C | Bound accepted trace writes for the fixture, declare C in records AND bytes including worst allowed site-id/path length, and declare drain behavior. No credit from a truncated/overflowed trace. |\n   323\t| Guest instruction ceiling and added work | Bound trace instructions per event/dispatch under each executed format, plus fixed setup/drain costs. Declare a ceiling for each host/format run before T; report baseline, absolute delta and ratio. |\n   324\t| Compile/expand/publish/verify/load/query time | Declare finite absolute time limits and allowed deltas against B/S in the preflight record. Pilot B/S measurements may set these; a tagged timeout is a failed bounded run. |\n   325\t| Peak process/heap/trace/index/continuation memory | Declare finite ceilings and measurement method; if a host lacks a heap counter, use a named process-memory measure and mark comparability limits. Missing measurement is not zero usage. |\n   326\t\n   327\tFor the oracle specifically, current code uses trace capacity **1,000,000 records**, drains after halt, and allows **4,000,000 guest instructions per C lane** (`latte_oracle_test.clj:1827,1847-1854,2453-2454`). These are the inspected baseline settings, not evidence the tagged run fits. Its own note records 2,024,912 walker and 1,105,792 semantic steps for the older binding fixture at line 2454. Restate both ceilings, the new record byte bound and the occupancy argument before T. If the implementation cannot establish enough capacity under those ceilings, publish revised bounds and their justification before running tagged evidence. Never silently raise fuel to get credit, or let a full trace stream park the fixture and misclassify it as semantic failure.\n   328\t\n   329\tFor other frontends, no oracle 4M/1M setting is inherited by default. Their adoption preflight must give numeric ceilings for each required fixture/prelude/host and format. Exceeding a declared bound blocks that acceptance run; changing bounds creates a new versioned run declaration and preserves the failed run.\n   330\t\n   331\t### 6.4 Budget impact allocated per frontend\n   332\t\n   333\t| Frontend | Mandatory static budget scope | Mandatory dynamic budget scope |\n   334\t|---|---|---|\n   335\t| Clojure | Native and argument-vector/outcome roots, macro outputs, guest library, linked `clj/yang.call`, repeated REPL admissions; `A_clj + L_clj + sum(P_f)` plus retained expansion/input closure | Nested/multi-arity/indirect/helper/tail calls in both production and oracle-specific fixtures; oracle owns its existing ceilings |\n   336\t| TypeScript | User units plus bundled and separately published `js/yang.call/jssp`; source→packet and packet→UAST timing separately; include post-seat publication additions | Constructor/member/indirect dispatch, exception helpers and admitted suspension paths; prelude/helper volume counted |\n   337\t| PHP | Both compiler families, includes/class-map/SCC, complete `php` including module/P9 definitions and shared runtime; peak publication closure | By-reference and indirect dispatch, include/autoload helpers, generator and exception paths |\n   338\t| Python | Fresh/primed session roots, imports/SCC, `py/yang.call/pysp`, site-set staging and DHT publication closure | Indirect descriptors, generated call dispatch, generators and hook/stream suspension paths |\n   339\t\n   340\tThe storage/work formulas are the design's budget impact; numbers require the pinned post-sweep corpus and are not asserted here. Shared `yang.call` must be reported once as retained shared content and separately as each frontend's dependency, avoiding both double charging and disappearance. Prelude republishing on four hosts is mandatory even when code hashes remain unchanged: the new occurrence/provenance artifacts need independent production/load evidence.\n852:+      (is (= :call-site-row\n853:+             (:rule (throws-ex-data\n854:+                      #(linearize/project-rows\n855:+                         bc nil [[[:oracle/fixture 1] root [] :yang/call-site 1]]))))))))\n858:+(deftest datom-lane-provenance-names-entities-only\n859:+  ;; cc3 item 4 (restriction): the datom lane's provenance stays\n860:+  ;; [pc entity]; it carries NO occurrence key K. The entity->occurrence\n861:+  ;; bridge is D1's stated dependency, recorded in the cc3 findings —\n862:+  ;; this lane must not silently grow a half-bridge.\n863:+  (let [d (datom-lane (app (v 'f) (lit 1)))]\n864:+    (is (every? (fn [row] (= 2 (count row))) (:provenance d)))\n865:+    (is (not (contains? d :call-provenance)))))\n  3205\t     :representation-seams\n  3206\t     {'kind/var? \"JVM Clojure Var predicate; explicitly declared, with no namespace lookup.\"\n  3207\t      'kind/with-meta \"Pure metadata attachment on the existing host value representation; the data ABI has no metadata-write export.\"}\n  3208\t     :context-fields {'latte-kernel.proof/+opacity-fn+ :opacity-policy}\n  3209\t     :fresh-supply-convention\n  3210\t     {:input {:counter 0} :allocation '(gensym supply prefix)\n  3211\t      :result '[symbol next-supply]\n  3212\t      :rebuild-type-result '[original-result next-context]\n  3213\t      :ambient-prefix-only :refused}\n  3214\t     :runtime {:clojure (clojure-version) :java (System/getProperty \"java.version\")}\n  3215\t     :instruction-budget-per-lane 4000000\n  3216\t     :instruction-budget-note \"The original uninstrumented fixtures used 1,000,000 instructions. Body-entry stream writes add guest instructions; traced fixtures have a 2,000,000 instruction bound. The harness drains only after halt. Under the D2 record lane the binding fixture's walker cell needs 2,024,912 steps (1.2% over 2M; semantic 1,105,792); the architect's 2026-11-04 ruling approves a uniform 4,000,000 acceptance budget (~1.98x headroom on the binding lane, measurement-supported, no per-fixture table). The attribution round's caller-site stamping adds one dispatcher call and one cell write per stamped guest call; every fixture in this evidence completed under the same 4,000,000 bound with the stamping active, and the trace stream bound stays stream/make 1000000 (one added field per body-entry record, no added records).\"\n  3217\t     :manifest-bindings (count manifest) :function-arity-candidates (count all-arities)\n  3218\t     :manifest-functions (count (filter :arities kernel-entries))\n  3219\t     :admitted-function-arity-count (count admitted-arities)\n  3220\t     :excluded-function-arity-count (- (count all-arities) (count admitted-arities))\n  3221\t     :binding-dispositions (frequencies (map :disposition manifest))\n  3222\t     :admission-note \"Manifest dispositions define the denominator independently of fixture success; excluded bindings retain explicit portability reasons.\"\n  3223\t     :program-status (if (empty? unexercised) :fixture-closure-complete :execution-evidence-incomplete)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
