{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"agent_message","text":"The core lowering and module-publication paths preserve executable bytes by inspection. The remaining blockers are in the surrounding guarantees: the oracle origin is reconstructed from a content hash, the REPL helper selects tables by root alone, and the preflight record omits the static-storage, time, and memory bounds required by §6.3. I’m separating those findings from the properties that pass."}}
