{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc | sed -n '430,446p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc | sed -n '370,383p'; nl -ba /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794357169000-engineer-cc3-lowering-provenance.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md | sed -n '294,308p'\"","aggregated_output":"   430\t                                                             [:bounds]))]))\n   431\t                            code-formats)]\n   432\t            (cond-> {:address address :manifest manifest\n   433\t                     :identities {:yin.semantic/code sem\n   434\t                                  :yin.debruijn.code sem\n   435\t                                  :yin.debruijn.register sem}\n   436\t                     :checksums {:yin.debruijn.code h\n   437\t                                 :yin.debruijn.register r}\n   438\t                     :links links}\n   439\t              call-sites (assoc :call-sites call-sites))))))))\n   440\t\n   441\t\n   442\t(defn publish-module!\n   443\t  \"Mint all four code formats, derivation records, and one schema-1 manifest.\n   444\t   `opts` `{:bounds {...}}` are the composition bounds (section 4.2 step\n   445\t   2) of every closure walk and local link the publication runs, every\n   446\t   bound left out taking `linker/default-bounds`. `opts` may also pin\n   370\t      (throw (ex-info \"Cannot project a program with a dangling root\" error)))\n   371\t    (when (nil? root-id)\n   372\t      (throw (ex-info \"Cannot project a program with no root\" {})))\n   373\t    (let [{:keys [code sources]} (flatten-tree (datom-reader get-attr)\n   374\t                                               root-id)]\n   375\t      {:vector code,\n   376\t       :address (ucf/code-address code),\n   377\t       :provenance (mapv (fn [pc [id _]] [pc id]) (range) sources)})))\n   294\t## Owner-visible items\n   295\t\n   296\t1. dht forwarding need (the cc2 custody item, closed on the publish side):\n   297\t   `dht/publish-name!` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/dht.cljc:70`) still\n   298\t   select-keyses `[:address :links]` and discards the publication result's\n   299\t   `:call-sites` handle - which now carries `:provenance` beside `:record`\n   300\t   and `:table`. dht.cljc is forbidden to this round, and the fix does NOT\n   301\t   require editing it: the publish side exposes the full retained handle\n   302\t   (`publish-closure!`'s result `:call-sites {:record ... :table ...\n   303\t   :provenance ...}`). The one-line forwarding need for the dht owner: add\n   304\t   `:call-sites` to dht.cljc:70's select-keys (or forward the record\n   305\t   address) so DHT publications retain their provenance handle.\n   306\t2. D1 dependency (the datom-lane restriction, item 4) - restated: the\n   307\t   entity-to-occurrence bridge is D1's to land; cc3's claims are row-lane\n   308\t   only.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed-GMT: 2026-11-11 05:12:44 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-11 12:12:44 ICT\n\nREVIEW VERDICT: REQUEST CHANGES\n\nStatic review only; no suites run and no files edited.\n\n1. **P1 | [latte_oracle_test.clj:3495](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3495) | Stamped paths are incorrectly reused as pre-stamp paths.**  \n   The binding combines the pre-stamp root with paths walked from the stamped tree. Stamping inserts three application wrappers around arguments ([line 2228](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2228)); descendants inside those arguments therefore move. A nested stamped site can resolve to a missing—or unrelated—pre-stamp application. Membership in `marked` ([line 3527](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3527)) proves only that an application exists there.  \n   **Required fix:** retain an explicit transformation mapping, or reconstruct paths by traversing both trees and removing recognized wrappers. Test nested argument sites and refuse mismatched or ambiguous correspondence.\n\n2. **P1 | [latte_oracle_test.clj:3472](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3472) | The oracle origin is synthesized from content, not recovered from an admission record.**  \n   `cc3-oracle-binding` takes `:canonical-source-hash`, constructs `[:source :program token 0]`, and creates a new envelope after compilation. `kernel-compile` retains the compiled AST and content hash, but no admission envelope ([line 2472](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2472)). Separate compilations of identical content consequently receive the same origin. Passing `occurrence-origin?` validates shape, not retained history.  \n   **Required fix:** record an admission coordinate when admitting the fixture, retain it with the compilation, and consume that record in the binding. Pin distinct admissions versus replay explicitly.\n\n3. **P1 | [repl.cljc:185](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:185) | Root-only lookup can borrow another admission’s provenance.**  \n   `packet-call-provenance` discards the admission component when selecting tables. If admission A has a retained C1 table and an unclaimed admission B has identical canonical content, B’s packet resolves using A’s table. The multiple-match refusal does not catch this single-match case. Existing admission tracking explicitly excludes assigning old evidence to new or unmapped programs ([line 1325](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1325)).  \n   **Required fix:** require the packet’s retained admission identity and select by `[admission root]`; return absence when that admission has no claim. Add the claimed-A/unclaimed-B identical-root regression.\n\n4. **P1 | [repl.cljc:168](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:168) | REPL provenance still is not persisted.**  \n   `packet->vector` still selects only `:vector`; all three production loaders continue through it ([line 277](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:277)). The new `packet-call-provenance` helper merely returns a computed map ([line 209](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:209)); its callers are tests. Its admission context remains session-only and disappears on rehydration ([line 1284](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1284)). Module publication is durable, but ordinary REPL loading still drops this relation.  \n   **Required fix:** connect admission-scoped provenance production to durable side-artifact retention and retain its lookup handle. Verify retrieval after reopening the store.\n\n5. **P2 | [latte_oracle_test.clj:3518](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3518) | Complete transformed coverage and instruction multiplicities are not established.**  \n   The complete-set comparison covers the pre-stamp tree, while execution uses the stamped tree. The findings explicitly distinguish 981 pre-stamp applications from 987 stamped applications ([findings:41](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794357169000-engineer-cc3-lowering-provenance.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md:41)). Native checks then compare sets of keys ([line 3551](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3551)), which discard multiplicity and do not independently establish complete semantic-call coverage.  \n   **Required fix:** verify the post-transformation application set, including inserted helpers, separately from selected oracle sites. Check exact call-PC coverage and multiplicities against independently derived expected occurrences, excluding Rule-R definitions.\n\n6. **P2 | [findings:21](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794357169000-engineer-cc3-lowering-provenance.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md:21) | The preflight record is incomplete under §6.3.**  \n   Counts are reported as compile-only measurements, but the record supplies no static-side storage/retained-memory bound, compilation/publication/verification time ceilings, or process/heap ceiling and measurement method. Those are explicit requirements at [design:321](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md:321).  \n   **Required fix:** record the missing measured quantities and finite ceilings before fresh tagged evidence. Preserve the earlier run’s incomplete-preflight status.\n\nRequested properties that passed by inspection:\n\n- **Per-occurrence lowering and silent absence:** `:call-provenance` joins `[root path]` to each validated row’s origin; missing rows produce no entry. Rule R emits no call row. [linearize.cljc:219](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc:219), [line 273](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc:273).\n- **Native PC reconstruction:** stack records the actual emission PC after child pushes; register derivation preserves instruction positions. Existing closure/variable diagnostic constructions remain intact. [derive.cljc:119](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc:119), [line 210](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc:210).\n- **Module persistence and canonical separation:** publication gates provenance on a C1 claim, removes register provenance before image materialization, and stores the relation outside the manifest. [publish.cljc:329](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:329), [line 355](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:355), [line 386](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:386).\n- **DHT custody exposure:** publication returns record, table, and provenance handles; the forwarding omission is accurately recorded. [publish.cljc:415](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc:415), [findings:296](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/yang-clojure/1794357169000-engineer-cc3-lowering-provenance.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md:296).\n- **Datom restriction:** explicitly documented and pinned by a test; no K bridge is claimed. [linearize.cljc:361](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc:361), [linearize_test.cljc:463](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/test/yin/vm/semantic/linearize_test.cljc:463).\n- **Zero added guest instructions:** the new binding is host-side analysis; existing 1,000,000-record and 4,000,000-instruction limits remain unchanged. [latte_oracle_test.clj:2454](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2454), [line 2484](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:2484), [line 3458](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3/test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:3458).\n- **Scope:** the tracked diff contains only the eight authorized files; none of the forbidden files changed."}}
